% dev/eval/expected.bib - hand-verified ground truth for the evaluation
% harness (dev/eval/run.py). Empty until populated by hand: every entry
% below must be checked against the PHYSICAL source, not a catalogue -
% populating this file is not something the pipeline, or anything short of
% actually reading each source, can do. See dev/eval/README.md.
%
% Format: ordinary BibLaTeX-Chicago entries (the same shape produced entries
% take), one per source in dev/eval/sample/. The citekey here must match
% that source's "citekey" in dev/eval/sample/manifest.json exactly - that is
% the only link between the two files.
%
%     @Article{Smith2020,
%       Author  = {Smith, Jane},
%       Title   = {A Title Exactly As It Should Extract},
%       ...
%     }
%
% Include every field the pipeline is expected to get right. Omit a field
% only when its correct value is genuinely unknowable from the source - the
% scorer then can't count its absence against a produced entry, but also
% can't reward a produced value that happens to be right; a source that
% itself states "n.d." or similar should still have that value recorded
% here, not be treated as unknowable.
%
% dev/eval/run.py scores each entry field-by-field against the pipeline's
% output for the same citekey; dev/eval/scorer.py is what actually compares
% them. Both are exercised without this file, or any real sample, by
% dev/eval/test_eval.py's synthetic fixture pair.
